        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(linux): support Cursor provider via app auth token",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nEnables `codexbar usage --provider cursor` on Linux by reading the signed-in Cursor app's access token from the XDG config state database and reusing the existing `cursor.com` usage endpoints.\n\nFixes the current Linux CLI behavior:\n\n```\nError: Cursor is only supported on macOS.\n```\n\n## Approach\n\n- Resolve Linux `state.vscdb` at `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/Cursor/User/globalStorage/state.vscdb` (default `~/.config/Cursor/...`)\n- Keep macOS browser cookie import and WebKit login flow unchanged\n- On Linux, auth order is: manual cookie header → cached session → Cursor app access token\n- Allow Linux CLI routing for Cursor instead of rejecting all web-source fetches up front\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Verified locally on Debian with Cursor installed and signed in\n- [ ] `swift test --filter CursorStatusProbeTests` on Linux CI\n- [ ] `codexbar usage --provider cursor --format json` on Linux\n\n## Notes\n\nAutomatic browser cookie import on Linux remains out of scope for this PR and can be a follow-up if SweetCookieKit paths are added.",
